                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "I had never heard of Killer Queen until I found the arcade cabinet at my local barcade and it quickly became my favorite game there. After the first time I played, I was almost puzzled the game was no longer available basically anywhere. To my surprise about a year later, I find the sequel has been quietly released on steam and FOR FREE.\n\nKiller Queen Black has a few changes/additions over the original version that I wasn't too sure about but quickly adapted to. More specifically, queens and warriors now have a dash attack button that allows for forward kills, meaning you no longer have to only be coming from above or behind to get kills. The other major change is workers now have the option to toss berries into the berry holes. It's a bit tricky but if you master it, it can quickly change the ride in an economy victory race.\n\nThis game is loads of fun, highly recommend.",
